WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.690
Hurricane Ian hits western
Cuba on 27 September 2022.

2
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:10.310
Then it strikes Cayo Costa,
Florida, at 130 knots.

3
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:16.150
At Fort Myers Beach, the surge
reached 3 to 4.6 metres above ground.

4
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:21.210
Damage in the United States:
112.9 billion dollars.

5
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:24.590
The United States is
a high-income economy.

6
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.460
Mozambique is low-income.

7
00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:29.870
So why can a storm cost
a rich country billions,

8
00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.670
yet kill far more people in a poor one?

9
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.730
Is that storm just stronger?

10
00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:38.550
In this mission, you'll sort
impacts into primary and secondary,

11
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.690
and follow Ian from forecast to recovery.

12
00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:46.010
Then you'll judge how well Florida's
forecasts and warnings worked.

13
00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:50.990
Your mission: explain why storms hit
rich and poor places so differently.
